=== FILE: evals/retrieval-quality/seed/raw/2026-04-27-vendor-split-announcement.md ===
From: Derek Blunt <dblunt@harborline.internal>
To: Juno Castillo <jcastillo@harborline.internal>
Cc: Victor Dunn <vdunn@harborline.internal>, Glenn Wexler <gwexler@harborline.internal>
Subject: RE: Pier 9 vendor assignments — Turnstile + Bridgeway

Juno, Victor —

Following Friday's scope session and a painful call with Kelwick, we're formally splitting vendors ahead of the single-contractor plan revision Victor's team is drafting.

**P9-GATE → Turnstile Dynamics**  
Gate automation, fare lane hardware, commissioning support. Turnstile is the **p9-gate vendor** going forward. Their PM is Alicia Varga; mobilization week of May 11 still plausible if we lock lane count.

**P9-GANG → Bridgeway Hoist**  
Gangway fabrication and hydraulic install. **Bridgeway Hoist** owns the **gangway replacement** scope as **p9-gang vendor**. Separate insurance cert, separate crane call if mock-up arrives before gate panels.

Kelwick stays on the old **pier 9 single-contractor** paperwork until Victor supersedes it — don't quote Kelwick in passenger notices after this email.

Glenn — two PO tracks means two change-order caps. I'll send Turnstile and Bridgeway quotes separately by Wednesday.

Victor — you still owe Marcus the night lighting circuit map for gate side only (gangway can run temp string lights per last call).

Sorry for the Monday morning wall of text. Coffee machine on 4th floor is still broken.

— Derek

